
oldjessie

This is a very old release of Debian.

It's used as an environment to build C/C++ programs, in order to link against 
old versions of system libraries. So, the result application can be run in 
most Linux boxes.

The docker image is built step by step, 
in each step, I operate in the docker running instance, 
rather than writing docker instructions and rebuild on that script.

So, the binary image can't be re-built, because there's no docker script.

-

    1. install
    
        Just pull from the docker hub official repo:
        docker run lenik/oldjessie
    
    2. maintaince
    
        future works on oldjessie can be done within the running instance,
        and push to docker hub.


